{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202467-as-above-so-below","id":1202467,"title":"As Above, So Below","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-02T23:55:10-07:00","id":1202467,"title":"As Above, So Below","content":"Since very few spells benefit substantially from additional successes, isn't this spell a bit weird? I mean, sure, you might get more exceptional successes, which is nice, but that doesn't match the fluff of the spell at all. I would expect bonus dice or rote quality instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:05:03-07:00","id":1202470,"title":"","content":"8-9 again and the rote quality is basically the same as bonus dice so your expectations are basically the same as what the spell does? Isnt this also a simple question, did it really need its own thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:11:29-07:00","id":1202471,"title":"","content":"No, because when spells only need 1 success to activate, 8-again and 9-again don't buy you anything. The rote quality lets you reroll failed dice, increasing the likelihood of your spell succeeding.<br /> <br /> Since the flavor of the spell is &quot;allow power to be harnessed more easily&quot;, it should actually do that IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:57:25-07:00","id":1202482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202467-as-above-so-below?p=1202471#post1202471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because when spells only need 1 success to activate, 8-again and 9-again don't buy you anything. The rote quality lets you reroll failed dice, increasing the likelihood of your spell succeeding.<br /> <br /> Since the flavor of the spell is &quot;allow power to be harnessed more easily&quot;, it should actually do that IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>More chance of a ES does mean you can <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">draw down power with greater facility</span></span> </div> </div> </div> since the benefits one can choose with a ES are worth it. The spell makes no mention of making the success of your spells greater merely that you can draw more power down which is then reflected in more chance of a ES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T01:00:31-07:00","id":1202484,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it\u2019s supposed to be an effect that facilitates ES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:36:08-07:00","id":1202764,"title":"","content":"One last thing - is this an intentional reduction from 1e then? In 1e, gaining 9-again or 8-again had the effect of boosting potency. In 2e, it just gives you more ES.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's why the Fate version lets you boost die pools... to make it better than the Prime version... hm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:39:13-07:00","id":1202767,"title":"","content":"It's intentional in the sense that they changed the system such that extra successes do no grant extra Potency to keep Mage in line with other CoD game lines where you only need 1 success to succeed at an action.<br /> <br /> Fate wasn't specifically written to make it better than Prime, it just so happens it has that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:58:06-07:00","id":1202780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202467-as-above-so-below?p=1202764#post1202764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that's why the Fate version lets you boost die pools... to make it better than the Prime version... hm...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is ample room to make the case that the Fate spell isn't supposed to give dice bonuses on spellcasting either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:57:08-07:00","id":1202805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202467-as-above-so-below?p=1202780#post1202780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is ample room to make the case that the Fate spell isn't supposed to give dice bonuses on spellcasting either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's unfortunate, although I see the ambiguity. I don't suppose Dave has weighed in on the intention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:34:32-07:00","id":1203077,"title":"","content":"I I'd allow Fate to give bonus dice on spellcasting (which I decide from game to game but usually do not), I'd allow a Prime ruling spell for only 1 reach instead of 2 as Prime should be more potent at influencing Supernal effects than Fate.<br /> <br /> Giving spellcasting rote quality is a Perfecting spell and as allways for rote quality costs a point of Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachment